 luffy has more of the pirate  king energy because he's just less  reactive he's at the cause and not the  effect  while law gets less caught up with the  competition between the other two  more like an introvert he's feeding some  birds on his own and he's  fine with riding on the same bird as  luffy he doesn't have to constantly  compete with him they say a picture is  worth a thousand words and with oda that  definitely applies  on to the chapter itself where we jump  right into the action this chapter is  called new onigashima project  so you know it's gonna spill some  important beans we start at the back  door of onigashima  where some of our guys are confronted by  the traitor kanjuro kundra obviously  knew that they'd be persistent and come  so he was ready for that we got plenty  of the red scabbars here to face kanjuro  including kawamatsu kiku rizo inuarashi  nekomamushi  ashura and even izo kundro says he won't  allow them to enter and he has a  sizeable team with him  so this is going to be one of the first  big group clashes of this war  our guys want to free momonosuke asap  and we get the story of what we've  already inferred before  kundra explains how momonosuke did his  best to free himself  he did take that knife he was looking at  freeing himself and tried to run away  when kundra tried to stop him momonosuke  stabbed him and then an angry kanjiro  beat the living daylights out of  momonosuke  kiku is clearly affected by this as are  the others even if they wear more stoic  expressions  kundru lets them know that momonosuke is  being publicly executed and that he just  has to stall them while the kozuki  bloodline disappears  it's funny how in the meantime inuarashi  and nekomamushi are having a  lighthearted combo about their new  modifications  it seems like nekomamushi has a gun  where his paw used to be i like that  they took this approach where they  turned something like losing a paw  into a kind of advantage like captain  hook but not evil and all  i can't help but respect these fighters  who injury after  injury keep coming back to fight again  mad respect for them kiku  then puts on an epic samurai helmet and  becomes the most  badass person ever kiku tells kundra to  shut up and sets and i quote you know  very well that the scars caused by my  blade  carry on to the afterlife right the  wound that i'm about to inflict on you  will torment your soul end quote that  must be one of the most epic lines  spoken in one piece  and i know the competition is stiff but  damn i  really love those words kiku attacks  kanjuro  and battling erupts we see that  inuarashi modified his legs into a blade  and now uses two sword style a very  creative way to fight and a style that's  very much at home  in the world of one piece we go back to  yamato and luffy  and we have some strong evidence that  yamato may well become the newest straw  hat member yamato straight up  asks if luffy will accept her on board  his ship here we might have some  translation issues but what appears to  happen is that luffy tells yamato  that she can't become odin odin was  another dude who was loved by many  people she can't just steal his identity  then yamato refers to luffy as odin  implying he  should then take on the role of the  legendary figure  from my perspective with this  translation it seems like yamato is  saying that someone needs to become odin  even if it's not her it's an interesting  idea where i suppose she's conflating  the need for someone to carry out odin's  will  with the need for odin himself let me  know your thoughts on this below  according to yamato with those shackles  she is not free  they may explode if she leaves and or  keep her from using her possible devil  fruit powers that would help her leave  yamato tells us that she wanted to leave  with ace  but since she was 8 she was forced to  stay on the island  interestingly enough luffy hasn't said  that yamato can't be a straw hat yet  he just said that s